## 🔬 Observed Day 4 Findings

### Lexical Dilution in TF-IDF

During production testing, we ran identical job descriptions against two variants of the same resume:
*   Original 1-page CV → **18.8%** TF-IDF Similarity
*   Expanded 3-page CV → **17.2%** TF-IDF Similarity

> [!NOTE]
> **Observation:** Longer documents do not necessarily produce higher TF-IDF similarity. Additional vocabulary and text bulk can actually *dilute* lexical alignment by increasing document length without proportionally increasing relevant keyword matches. 
> 
> *This is a critical finding that validates our decision to use a multi-faceted Provisional Score rather than relying entirely on TF-IDF.*

### 🛡️ Privacy Verification

A complete audit of the live Streamlit logs verified that our privacy promises are upheld in production. 

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Privacy Audit:** Production logs successfully recorded extraction metadata (e.g., character counts and pipeline status events), but **no extracted resume text or PII** was dumped to the logs.

